  "headline": "NAB's cash cost-to-income ratio (CTI) rose 0.8 ppt to 47.3% in FY25 from 46.5% in FY24, driven by expense growth of 4.6% outpacing revenue growth of 2.9%. On a statutory basis, CTI rose 1.1 ppt to 49.6% from 48.5%. The widening gap between expense and income growth reflects $130 million in payroll review and remediation costs, higher personnel expenses (+4.8%), technology costs (+3.5%), and general expenses (+6.8%), partially offset by $420 million of productivity benefits.",
