      "columns": "Sep 24 to Sep 25",
      "narrative": "Operating expenses rose $435 million or 4.6% to $9,848 million from $9,413 million. Excluding $130 million of payroll review and remediation costs, expenses grew 3.2%. Personnel expenses increased $271 million or 4.8% to $5,860 million, driven by salary inflation, investment in additional bankers and resources, and technology/financial crime capabilities, partially offset by $420 million of productivity benefits. Technology expenses rose $71 million or 3.5% to $2,105 million due to software licences, maintenance and cloud consumption. General expenses increased $81 million or 6.8% to $1,280 million, primarily from continued technology investment, partially offset by productivity benefits.",
